---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article class="shell narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Sabiqah</p>
    <h1>Open review without hiding uncertainty.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Sabiqah is a reader and contribution interface. Each book repository remains the canonical
      scholarly record, and maintainers review proposed changes in public pull requests.
    </p>
    <h2>Everyone may review</h2>
    <p>
      Enrolled participants may propose translations, corrections, and evidence. Enrollment does
      not grant merge access. Automated quality assessment can help triage work, but humans remain
      responsible for scholarly decisions and access restrictions.
    </p>
    <h2>Arabic stays protected</h2>
    <p>
      Ordinary translation review cannot overwrite Arabic. A source correction is a separate,
      evidence-backed proposal with visible provenance and protected maintainer review.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
